<title>USA: United Tech's Pratt lays off 450 workers.</title>
<headline>United Tech's Pratt lays off 450 workers.</headline>
<dateline>HARTFORD 1997-02-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Jet engine maker Pratt &amp; Whitney, a unit of United Technologies Corp., on Friday said it laid off 450 salaried employees in Connecticut and Florida.</p>
<p>The layoffs were evenly split between the two states, Pratt spokesman Mark Sullivan told Reuters.</p>
<p>&quot;We expect layoffs will continue at Pratt as we work to become the lowest-cost manufacturer of aircraft gas turbines,&quot; Sullivan said. He declined to provide specific figures or a time frame.</p>
</text>
